Figure \ref{fig:consensus} shows consensus achievement in a $4$-agent system with expanded interaction range ($\epsilon=1, \alpha=0.5$). The simulation results verify that when all initial opinions fall within the neighborhood threshold, the fractional-order HK model (\ref{model:HKfrac}) guarantees asymptotic global consensus.

