\\
Up to this stage, we shall point out that this construction reveals that the relativistic Lagrangian (Hamiltonian) and EOM can be understood as \emph{emergent structures} which is not by imposing relativity externally, but by integrating over a parameter space of generalized classical models. This offers a novel bottom-up perspective: just as macroscopic thermodynamic laws emerge from microscopic statistical behavior, relativistic dynamics can emerge from hidden structure embedded in non-relativistic mechanics.
