\section{Results}
 Pulses recorded at the N1 peaks (Fig.\,\ref{fig:pulses}) in the two implanted arrays are well described by a double exponential model with a rise and fall time. 
 However, a slight deviation from the simple exponential behavior is observed at the start of the decay, likely due to the breakdown of the small signal approximation. Furthermore, aside from the primary exponential decay time constants, which range between approximately 600\,\mus\ and 900\,\mus, no additional long time constants correlated with the implanted activities are observed in the pulses.

