\vspace{0.5em}
\noindent \textbf{Worst-Case Queuing Delay ($\mathrm{d_{queue}^i}$):} The frames experience queuing delay in the switch along the route. This delay represents the total amount of time the TT flow frames spend waiting in the egress port queue before transmission. The maximum queuing delay of a TT flow $f_i$, denoted as $\mathrm{d_{queue}^i}$, depends on the \texttt{QG} of the flow and its cycle. Therefore, we express $\mathrm{d_{queue}^i}$ in terms of the cycle as follows:
\vspace{-0.1cm}
\begin{equation}
  \mathrm{d_{queue}^i} =
    \begin{cases}
      T_{\texttt{QG}x} & , \forall \; f_i \in \texttt{QG}x, \; \text{if \texttt{QG}x has 3 Queues,} \\
      0  & , \; \mathrm{otherwise}. \\
    \end{cases}
    \label{eq:dqueue}
\end{equation}
\noindent where $x = 1,2,3$ for TT flows belonging to \texttt{QG}1, \texttt{QG}2, and \texttt{QG}3 respectively.

