 As a numerical example, consider the total number of families over $\Q_p$ with degree 
 $p^2$.  There is just one family with ramification index $e=1$, the unramified family $(\;)^{p^2}$.  There
 are $p$ families with $e=p$, the geometric families $(1)^p$, $(2)^p$, \dots, $(p-1)^p$ and the
 arithmetic family $(p)^p$.  Guided by Figure~\ref{fig families}, one can check that there are
