\subsection{Mean Squared Displacement}
The Mean Squared Displacement reveals a lot about the single particle dynamics of a many-body system. In glassy systems, the MSD exhibits a plateau region \cite{chong2001mean, deng2019configuration}. 
The observed change in the static structure as shown by the RDF, C2P and intra-shell angular correlation function with increase in coupling strength (i.e, the splitting up of the 2nd peak of RDF and the intra-shell angular correlation function)  motivates us to examine the Mean Squared Displacement (MSD) around this range of $\Gamma$ values.

